{"authors": [], "discovered_at": "2026-11-02T02:18:08.318527Z", "id": "github:release:535360445:release:430975938", "kind": "release", "matched_terms": [], "metadata": {"action": "released", "draft": false, "forks": 11956, "prerelease": false, "stars": 63022, "stars_delta": 13, "tag_name": "v8.4.198"}, "organization": "ultralytics", "priority": {"source": 0.5}, "published_at": "2026-11-02T01:14:07Z", "related_items": [], "scores": {}, "source": "github", "source_id": "535360445:release:430975938", "summary": "## \ud83c\udf1f Summary\n**Ultralytics 8.4.198 makes training settings and YAML files more reliable, alongside fixes to downloads, dataset errors, and documentation.** No model architecture or pretrained-weight changes are included.\n\n## \ud83d\udcca Key Changes\n- **NumPy learning rates now save correctly in YAML** \u2014 The main change converts `np.float64` values to ordinary numeric values when writing YAML. Training arguments such as sweep-generated learning rates can now be saved and reused from `args.yaml`.\n- **More robust YAML parsing** \u2014 Fixes handling of block-scalar indentation, whitespace-only lines, and nodes written on their own lines, bringing the built-in parser closer to YAML conventions.\n- **Improved download and dataset errors** \u2014 Downloads now identify themselves with an Ultralytics User-Agent, helping avoid some servers rejecting requests. Missing classification datasets now produce a clear file-not-found error instead of a confusing failed-download message.\n- **More dependable training and logging** \u2014 Updates the minimum supported versions of `ultralytics-thop` and `ultralytics-platform`; also suppresses a Triton warning that could appear during profiling.\n- **Clearer documentation** \u2014 Explains how relative `project` paths are resolved and standardizes how metrics such as mAP and depth accuracy are written across docs and benchmark tables.\n\n## \ud83c\udfaf Purpose & Impact\n- \ud83d\udd01 **Reuse training configurations more easily:** NumPy-based hyperparameter sweeps no longer produce YAML values that reload as strings and fail validation.\n- \ud83e\uddf0 **Fewer confusing failures:** YAML parsing, downloads, and missing-dataset handling are more predictable.\n- \ud83d\udcda **Easier to follow guidance and compare results:** Consistent metric labels and clarified path behavior reduce ambiguity.\n- \u2705 **No model migration needed:** These updates improve tooling and documentation rather than changing model behavior.\n\n## What's Changed\n* Document that a relative `project` goes under `runs_dir/<task>` by @Echoslayer in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26985\n* Fix block scalar indentation, space-only lines and own-line node indents in the YAML parser by @cainiao33 in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26987\n* Remove UTF-8 BOM handling by @glenn-jocher in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26988\n* Silence Triton 3.9 FP fusion default warning from torch 2.15 eager bmm by @glenn-jocher in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26989\n* Write every metric with explicit sub/superscripts: mAP<sub>50-95</sub>, \u03b4<sub>1</sub>, mAP<sup>val</sup><sub>50-95</sub> by @glenn-jocher in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26990\n* Require ultralytics-thop>=2.2.4 and ultralytics-platform>=0.1.102 by @glenn-jocher in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26991\n* Send a descriptive User-Agent on downloads and report missing classify data clearly by @glenn-jocher in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26992\n* `ultralytics 8.4.198` Save NumPy float64 values as numbers in YAML files by @Nikhi00718 in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26993\n\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/compare/v8.4.197...v8.4.198\n", "title": "ultralytics/ultralytics v8.4.198 - `ultralytics 8.4.198` Save NumPy float64 values as numbers in YAML files (#26993)", "topics": ["image_classification", "instance_segmentation", "object_detection", "object_tracking", "semantic_segmentation"], "updated_at": "2026-11-02T01:15:32Z", "url": "https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/releases/tag/v8.4.198", "venue": null}
{"authors": [], "discovered_at": "2026-11-02T02:18:08.318527Z", "id": "github:release:535360445:release:430317752", "kind": "release", "matched_terms": [], "metadata": {"action": "released", "draft": false, "forks": 11956, "prerelease": false, "stars": 63022, "stars_delta": 13, "tag_name": "v8.4.197"}, "organization": "ultralytics", "priority": {"source": 0.5}, "published_at": "2026-11-01T02:29:38Z", "related_items": [], "scores": {}, "source": "github", "source_id": "535360445:release:430317752", "summary": "## \ud83c\udf1f Summary\n**Ultralytics 8.4.197 makes AMP checks work without downloading model weights and removes PyYAML from the base dependencies.** \ud83d\ude80\n\n## \ud83d\udcca Key Changes\n- **AMP checks no longer download a checkpoint.** The check builds an untrained YOLO26n from its YAML config and compares FP32 and AMP results across convolution and attention layers.\n- **AMP checks are more independent of training setup.** They check the model\u2019s device without relying on pretrained weights, internet access, or resetting callbacks.\n- **Ultralytics now includes its own minimal YAML reader and writer.** It supports the YAML structures commonly used in Ultralytics configs, datasets, and export metadata. PyYAML is no longer a required base dependency.\n- **Documentation examples now use `ultralytics.utils.YAML`** to save YAML files.\n\n## \ud83c\udfaf Purpose & Impact\n- \ud83d\udcf4 **Smoother offline training:** AMP checks can run without downloading weights, avoiding unexpected network requests and skipped checks.\n- \ud83d\udee1\ufe0f **More reliable AMP validation:** Comparing individual layers helps identify precision issues before AMP is used for training.\n- \ud83d\udce6 **Simpler installation:** Removing PyYAML from the base requirements reduces a dependency for standard installs. The built-in parser covers Ultralytics\u2019 common YAML needs, but it is not intended to support every YAML feature.\n- \ud83d\udcc4 **More consistent YAML handling:** Users can use the same built-in utility to load and save supported Ultralytics YAML files.\n\n## What's Changed\n* Replace PyYAML with a minimal built-in YAML parser by @glenn-jocher in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26983\n* `ultralytics 8.4.197` Check AMP on an untrained YOLO26n without downloading weights by @glenn-jocher in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26967\n\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/compare/v8.4.196...v8.4.197\n", "title": "ultralytics/ultralytics v8.4.197 - `ultralytics 8.4.197` Check AMP on an untrained YOLO26n without downloading weights (#26967)", "topics": ["image_classification", "instance_segmentation", "object_detection", "object_tracking", "semantic_segmentation"], "updated_at": "2026-11-01T02:31:03Z", "url": "https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/releases/tag/v8.4.197", "venue": null}
